// Biomes (plan §13.1), their scatter (§13.2) and the set pieces each favours (§7.5). Along the line, biomes change in
// regions of regionKm with transitionM blends; a route's region (its most common biome) sets the piece bias.
// ground: the base splat material (§12.5), a texture library name; materials[0]: what it gives way to, on the steep and
// in patches (granite outcrops on the barrens, red clay cut banks in the valley farmland: the Maritimes' two tells); noiseScale multiplies tiers.json's
// terrain noise; treeDensity: trees per 100 m2 of ground past treesFromM; deadTrees: the share dead; water: how
// likely low ground holds standing water; colour: the ground's greybox colour (sRGB 0..1), from the GDD §27 palette.
// The country is Nova Scotia gone dark. flora: the living trees' kinds by weight (spruce, fir, birch, pine: white pine standing over the rest, tamarack: gold in the bogs; the dead ones are
// ghost spruce and bare snags, by deadTrees); rocks: boulders per 12 m of line; verge: what grows along it (grass,
// reeds, barrens); props: per 150 m of line, the chance of each piece, how far out, and how many (the art's
// WorldArt.PlanDressing: saltbox, barn, church, buryingGround, fishShed, stoneWall, orchard, oldField, erratic, outcrop, ruin,
// chimney, tank, headframe). landform: the land's shape as a mix of tiers.json's terrain landforms (rolling, drumlins,
// knobs, plateau). The Maritimes' water and line (docs/design/maritime-rules.md): lakesPerKm, how often a lake lies
// by the line; shore, the chance the line keeps to a shore here, and shoreKind (sea: the Atlantic's rock and coves;
// fundy: red mudflats; dyke: a dyked marsh; river: a river alongside, the line up its valley); sweepChance, how often a connector curves (a coast line heads every cove);
// tidalRivers: its rivers are tidal, wide mud banks under long trusses; roads: the chance a region has a country road
// beside the line (tiers.json terrain.roads), with its homesteads and level crossings. ballast (a texture; default the
// granite "ballast") and ballastTint: the bed's stone in this country (GDD §30): cinders through the coal country, pale on
// the barrens, peat-stained in the bog, tarred black in the tar ponds.
